---
import { INSTALL_COMMAND, PROOF } from '../lib/site';
import Button from './Button.astro';
---
<div class="rt-install">
  <div class="rt-install-row">
    <code id="install-cmd">{INSTALL_COMMAND}</code>
    <button type="button" data-copy-target="#install-cmd">Copy install command</button>
    <span class="rt-sr-only" aria-live="polite" data-copy-live></span>
  </div>
  <p class="rt-install-note">
    Needs <code>uv</code> or <code>pipx</code>, <code>git</code>, Python 3.11+ and a signed-in Claude
    Code. Not on PyPI. The repo documents two slower paths, and why you might want them:
  </p>
  <div class="rt-btn-row">
    <Button href={PROOF.verify} external>Verify the checksum first</Button>
    <Button href={PROOF.clone} external>Clone and read it</Button>
  </div>
  <p class="rt-install-note">
    <b>What that one-liner gives you:</b> the installer pins <code>v0.6.0</code>, so it does not
    install the enforced stages or the independent plan review described above — those are newer
    than that tag. To run them, clone the repository and install from <code>main</code>.
  </p>
</div>
